Package: caliber
Type: Package
Title: Monotone Calibration of a Digital Measure to a Multi-Item PRO
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-10-14
Authors@R: person("Paolo", "Eusebi", email = "paoloeusebi@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Places the item thresholds of an ordinal multi-item
    patient-reported outcome (PRO) on the scale of a continuous digital or
    performance measure. One latent trait drives both instruments: the PRO
    items follow a logistic graded response model (GRM), and the digital
    measure depends on the trait through a non-increasing cubic B-spline with
    log-linear residual SD, fitted by monotonic likelihood boosting
    (Leitenstorfer and Tutz 2007) with the AIC stop, or alternatively by
    Ramsay's (1988) monotone regression splines (I-splines with non-negative
    coefficients, fitted by maximum likelihood). The measure can be
    continuous (Gaussian) or a count (Poisson or negative binomial, with the
    spline on the log mean). Three ways of handling
    the latent trait are implemented: concurrent calibration (MS-Joint),
    EAP plug-in (MS-EAP) and fixed-item calibration (MS-Fixed). Outputs are
    thresholds in the digital measure's units, structural and probabilistic
    crosswalks, exceedance probabilities, Wright maps, and hybrid intervals
    (normal-approximation draws for item and threshold quantities,
    nonparametric bootstrap for the curve).
